  2| //! reviewed and what is new.
  3| //!
  4| //! The rendering lives here rather than in a lane because two callers need the
  5| //! *same bytes*: the lane, which sends them, and `review`, which stores them so
  6| //! the next cycle can replay them. Prompt layer 3 only pays if the replay is
  7| //! byte-identical (see `crate::harness::prompt`), and two independent renderers
  8| //! would drift apart on the first formatting change and silently cost every
  9| //! re-review full input price.
 10| //!
 11| //! The split is per file. A file whose rendered block is unchanged since the
 12| //! last review has already been reviewed, so it goes in the cacheable prefix;
 13| //! anything else is the delta and goes in the volatile suffix. Per file rather
 14| //! than per commit because a pull request diff is what the forge gives us —
 15| //! there is no local checkout to compute a commit range against.
